notes: >
  A newly ADDED generator directive whose output is missing must FAIL the drift gate, not skip —
  hiding exactly the codegen a change introduces. Under the clean-tree precondition (D-STACK-017)
  new files arrive as commits, so the directive lives in a committed file on the work branch; the
  gate writes gen.out in the real tree and the guard rolls it back after the verdict.
requires: [go]
commit:
  gen.go: "package main\n\n//go:generate sh -c \"printf fresh > gen.out\"\n"
argv: ['--all']
exitCode: 1
gates:
  golang:generate:
    status: fail
    outputIncludes: ['gen.out']
